AGIConstructor — Licensing
===========================

This repository is dual-licensed. Which license applies depends on the kind of
file. This split is intentional: the written standards are meant to be cited and
built on, while the machine-readable artifacts are meant to be freely reused in
software.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. WRITTEN STANDARDS AND DOCTRINE  —  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC BY 4.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Applies to the prose documents:

    ACL-1.0.md
    FOUNDATION_DOCTRINE.md
    CONSTRUCTION_ONTOLOGY.md
    ARCHITECTURE.md
    ACL-2.0-CANDIDATES.md
    README.md
    examples/example-ledger.md

You are free to share and adapt these documents for any purpose, including
commercially, under the terms of CC BY 4.0, provided you give appropriate credit
(a citation), link to the license, and indicate if changes were made.

Full text: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode
Summary:   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Suggested citation:
    ACL-1.0 — AGI Component Ledger. AGIConstructor.com, 2026.

Independent use of the ACL protocol itself: ACL-1.0 §9 grants that the protocol
"may be applied, cited, reproduced, and published by any party without permission
or notification," and that derived ledgers need not be shared with the
maintainer. That grant governs application of the protocol; the CC BY 4.0 terms
above govern reproduction and adaptation of the document text. The only condition
for calling a result an ACL audit remains procedural (ACL-1.0 §9).

